    fix(trials): a dismissed trial sheet for another plan never uses up the offered trial (B-673-3)
    
    A client opens package A's free-trial sheet, dismisses it without saving a
    card, then opens package B of the same coach. The offer for B said the trial
    was available, but checkout sold B with no trial because A's unstarted open
    attempt still held the one trial (the stale-attempt cleanup only reached
    attempts older than 23 h).
    
    A checkout for a plan that offers a trial now retires an unstarted trial
    attempt for another plan of the same coach at any age, through the same
    Stripe-confirmed retire path (no card saved: the SetupIntent is canceled and
    the subscription ended, then the row is expired). B gets the trial its offer
    showed. Unchanged: same-plan resume (this plan's own attempt keeps the reuse
    window), started trials, and an attempt whose card was saved (still holds
    the trial).
    
    Tests: Sol's offer-vs-checkout test in test/b-trials-8-shared-rule.spec.ts
    (failed before), a same-plan resume control, and main's R1-1 another-package
    test split into the no-card (retired, trial given) and card-saved (still
    held) cases.

